Define the Lustre element types that users write in their view functions.

## Why Separate from Reconciler
Element types are the user-facing API. Keep them stable and well-documented separately from the reconciler internals.

## API (Gleam)
```gleam
// Core element type
type Element(msg)

// Constructors
fn box(attrs: List(Attribute(msg)), children: List(Element(msg))) -> Element(msg)
fn text(attrs: List(Attribute(msg)), content: String) -> Element(msg)
fn span(attrs: List(Attribute(msg)), content: String) -> Element(msg)  // Inline text

// Future: Input elements
// fn input(attrs: List(Attribute(msg))) -> Element(msg)
// fn button(attrs: List(Attribute(msg)), label: String) -> Element(msg)

// Attributes - Layout
fn width(size: Size) -> Attribute(msg)
fn height(size: Size) -> Attribute(msg)
fn flex_direction(dir: FlexDirection) -> Attribute(msg)
fn justify_content(j: Justify) -> Attribute(msg)
fn align_items(a: Align) -> Attribute(msg)
fn padding(p: Int) -> Attribute(msg)
fn padding_xy(x: Int, y: Int) -> Attribute(msg)
fn margin(m: Int) -> Attribute(msg)
fn gap(g: Int) -> Attribute(msg)

// Attributes - Style
fn fg(color: String) -> Attribute(msg)  // "#8aadf4"
fn bg(color: String) -> Attribute(msg)
fn bold() -> Attribute(msg)
fn dim() -> Attribute(msg)
fn underline() -> Attribute(msg)
fn border(style: BorderStyle) -> Attribute(msg)

// Attributes - Events (for input elements)
fn on_click(msg: msg) -> Attribute(msg)
fn on_key(handler: fn(Key) -> Option(msg)) -> Attribute(msg)
```

## Design Decisions
- Attributes are typed to msg for event handlers
- Colors are strings (parsed by tui_core/color)
- Sizes use the same Size type as Renderables
- Keep API minimal initially, expand based on needs

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] box/text/span constructors work
- [ ] All layout attributes defined
- [ ] All style attributes defined
- [ ] Event attribute types defined (even if not implemented)
- [ ] Types compile and are ergonomic to use

